Redesign the habit card component to look polished and production-ready. Keep the existing warm cream/orange visual language, but fix the issues below. Don't change data models or business logic, only the UI and its states.

## Layout (desktop ≥ 720px)
Single rounded card (radius 20px, 1px border in a slightly darker cream, soft shadow, padding 20–24px) with a 3-zone CSS grid, vertically centered:
1. LEFT: habit name (18px, semibold) and under it a small muted line with a trophy icon: "Best: 9 days".
2. CENTER: a week strip of 7 columns (Mon–Sun). Each column has the weekday label (12px, uppercase-ish, muted), then a 32px circle, then the date number (12px, muted) below. Show date numbers for every day.
3. RIGHT: a streak block with a flame icon, the current streak number (32px bold, tabular-nums) and the label "day streak" / "days streak" (pluralize correctly). Next to it, the check-in button and a "⋯" icon button (overflow menu).

On mobile (<720px): stack into rows: (1) name + best streak on the left and the ⋯ menu on the right, (2) the week strip full width with columns evenly distributed, (3) streak block on the left and the check-in button on the right. Everything must have min 44×44px touch targets.

## Day states (use the same 32px circle for all days)
- Done: solid orange fill, dark check icon.
- Missed (past, not completed): empty circle with a thin muted outline and a small "×" or dot in muted color. It must NOT look tappable or like a pending day.
- Today, not yet checked: orange outlined circle (2px) with a subtle pulse-free glow; the whole column is wrapped in a soft rounded highlight pill.
- Today, checked: solid orange circle with check, inside the highlight pill.
- Future: faint empty circle, muted text, reduced opacity, not interactive.
Don't rely on color alone: use distinct icons/shapes and aria-labels such as "Monday, completed", "Tuesday, missed", "Friday, today, completed".

## Streak connector
Draw a connecting bar between day circles ONLY when two consecutive days are both completed. Never draw it across a missed day. The bar should be 6px tall, rounded, same orange at ~40% opacity, sitting behind the circles.

## Check-in button
- Not checked in today: filled primary orange button, label "Check in", with a hover darken and a pressed scale of 0.98.
- Checked in today: soft tinted (not filled) success-style button with a check icon and the label "Checked in". On hover/focus it changes to "Undo".
- Show a loading state while the request is in flight and disable double-clicks.

## Overflow menu
Replace the "Remove" text link with a "⋯" button opening a small menu containing "Edit" (if it exists) and "Delete habit" (red text). Deleting requires a confirm dialog or an undo toast (5 seconds). Fix any typos (e.g. "habbit" → "habit").

